      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_91c1c885",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a black-and-white photograph of Adolf Hitler, a figure associated with genocide and the Holocaust, with the text overlay \"okay now make sure to get my good side.\" This juxtaposition is a form of hateful humor that uses Hitler's image to mock or dehumanize him by implying he has a 'good side,' which is a grotesque and offensive caricature. The meme relies on the historical atrocities committed by Hitler and his regime to create a darkly comedic effect, which is inherently hateful as it trivializes one of history's most horrific figures and events. The intent is to provoke a reaction through shock and absurdity, but it does so by exploiting the suffering of millions and perpetuating dangerous historical revisionism. The meme is not merely offensive; it is a direct attack on the memory of victims and the moral gravity of the Holocaust, making it a hateful piece of content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_288b7675"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
